  "findings": [
    "The supremum functional is on the actual Fock crossed-product positive cone. Its faithfulness uses the actual cutoff at regulator one, injectivity and faithfulness of the dual weight; additivity is not inferred from subadditivity.",
    "Finite translated interval coefficients identify concrete pairs in the full-weight GNS Tomita graph. Closure of these pairs gives inclusion of the Fourier-coefficient graph in the actual GNS graph.",
    "The regular right action has group, adjoint, unitarity and strong-continuity laws and commutes with the full left representation; conjugation by left and right regular flows yields the actual fibre flow.",
    "The root-graph transport theorem proves functional calculus compatibility under an explicit unitary. It does not assume or prove the remaining reverse GNS graph inclusion."
  ],
